  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving First Responders&apos; Management of GBV Cases in Mauritius</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to strengthen the capacity of Mauritian law enforcement to respond effectively to domestic abuse (DA) and gender-based violence (GBV). The proposed activities will result in a cohort of officers trained in best practice responses, improved inter-agency coordination, and survivor-centred approaches. These outputs directly support the project&#x2019;s purpose: to improve the quality and consistency of law enforcement responses to DA and GBV in Mauritius.</narrative>
  </description>
